      "message": "`ByteStream::from_path` and `ByteStream::read_from()` now read files with a 64 KiB buffer by default, up from 4 KiB. On a 64 MiB file this makes reads about 5x faster (174 to 899 MiB/s in the new `bytestream_from_file` benchmark). Each open file stream uses about 60 KiB more memory. To keep the old behavior, call `ByteStream::read_from().buffer_size(4096)`.\n",
